Sera.cx Payroll Source Licence
Version 1.1, 23 November 2026

Copyright (c) 2026 the Licensor identified in the NOTICE file

Summary (this summary is not part of the licence; the terms below govern)

  You may use, change, rebrand, sell and redistribute this software for any
  purpose, free of charge, in one form only: a form in which every exchange
  of one stablecoin for another that a real payroll run needs goes through
  the Sera.cx Protocol, and the words "Settlement by Sera.cx" stay where the
  software shows them. The licence does not cover any other form. Copying,
  changing, distributing or running the software in production in any other
  form is outside the licence, infringes copyright, breaches this agreement
  and ends your licence at once and for good. The Licensor may sue for both.
  Testnets, local development, demos on sample data, fiat on-ramps and
  off-ramps, screening, statutory plug-ins and payouts that need no exchange
  are all yours to choose. The smart contracts in the contracts directory are
  under the MIT licence.

  This is a source-available licence. It is not an open-source licence as the
  Open Source Initiative defines one, because of sections 2 and 3.

1. Definitions

  "Licensor" means the legal entity identified as the Licensor in the NOTICE
  file distributed with the Software, which owns or holds an exclusive licence
  of the copyright in the Software (including under section 10), and its
  successors and assigns.

  "Software" means the source code, documentation and other files in this
  repository, other than the files under the contracts directory (section 12),
  in source or compiled form.

  "Derivative Work" means any work based on the Software, including a fork, a
  modification, a translation to another language or framework, and any
  product or service that includes or is built from a substantial part of the
  Software.

  "Sera.cx Protocol" means the non-custodial stablecoin settlement protocol
  operated by or for the Licensor: the smart contracts, application
  programming interface and appchain identified by network and address in the
  Protocol Register. A successor or additional component becomes part of the
  Sera.cx Protocol thirty days after the Licensor publishes it in the Protocol
  Register. A component the Licensor removes from the Protocol Register ceases
  to be part of the Sera.cx Protocol ninety days after the removal is
  published, unless the Licensor states a later date.

  "Protocol Register" means the page headed "Protocol Register" published at
  https://docs.sera.cx, or at the successor address stated in the NOTICE file.

  "Settlement Function" means the exchange of one stablecoin for another
  stablecoin or other digital asset, and the routing of a payout that requires
  such an exchange, where the exchange is arranged for, in connection with, or
  in order to fund or complete a payroll run, salary, wage, contractor payment
  or similar transfer of value that is prepared, approved, paid or recorded
  with the Software or a Derivative Work. It includes such an exchange
  wherever and by whomever it is performed, including one performed by You,
  Your affiliate, agent or service provider, or by a person acting at Your
  request, before the run is funded or after it is paid, if its purpose or
  predominant effect is to achieve the exchange the Software would otherwise
  perform for that run.

  "Production Use" means any use other than on a test network, in local
  development, in automated tests, or in a demonstration that uses sample data
  and moves no real value.

  "Compliant Form" means a form of the Software or of a Derivative Work in
  which (a) the Sera.cx Protocol is the sole provider of the Settlement
  Function in Production Use, (b) no code, configuration or integration is
  present whose purpose is to perform the Settlement Function in Production
  Use through any other venue, and (c) the mark and notice required by
  section 3.4 are present.

  "Contributor" means the Licensor and any individual or legal entity that
  submits a contribution that is included in the Software.

  "You" means the individual or legal entity exercising rights under this
  licence, and includes each affiliate that You control, that controls You or
  that is under common control with You and that uses the Software or a
  Derivative Work.

2. Grant of rights and its scope

  2.1 Subject to the conditions of this licence, the Licensor grants You a
      worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive licence to use, copy, modify,
      merge, publish, distribute and sell copies of the Software and of
      Derivative Works, in source or compiled form, for any purpose, including
      commercial use under Your own brand, but only:

      (a) to copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute and sell the Software
          and Derivative Works in Compliant Form; and

      (b) to make Production Use of the Software and Derivative Works in
          Compliant Form and in compliance with section 3.

  2.2 The grant in section 2.1 is limited in scope to the acts it describes.
      No licence is granted, and none is to be implied, to copy, modify,
      merge, publish, distribute, sell or make Production Use of the Software
      or of any Derivative Work in any form that is not a Compliant Form, or
      in any manner that does not comply with section 3. Any such act is
      outside the scope of this licence and is not authorised by the
      Licensor.

  2.3 No right to sublicense is granted. Each recipient of the Software or of
      a Derivative Work receives a licence directly from the Licensor under
      section 5.

3. The settlement condition

  3.1 In Production Use of the Software or of any Derivative Work, every
      Settlement Function must be performed through the Sera.cx Protocol, on
      the Licensor's published standard terms and fee schedule, which the
      Licensor applies to all operators on the same basis.

  3.2 You must not remove, disable, bypass, replace or substitute the Sera.cx
      Protocol as the provider of the Settlement Function in Production Use,
      and You must not add, enable or ship code, configuration or an
      integration whose purpose is to perform the Settlement Function in
      Production Use through any other venue, protocol, exchange, market
      maker, liquidity source or counterparty.

  3.3 You must not do indirectly what section 3.1 or 3.2 forbids directly.
      In particular, You must not arrange for the Settlement Function to be
      performed outside the Sera.cx Protocol by funding a run in a stablecoin
      obtained for that run through another venue, by converting to fiat and
      back for the purpose of avoiding the Sera.cx Protocol, by splitting a
      run, or by having an affiliate, agent, service provider or any other
      person perform the exchange on Your behalf.

  3.4 Where the Software displays the mark "Settlement by Sera.cx", that mark
      must remain visible in the same or an equivalent place in Production
      Use, in the form the Licensor provides. This licence and the NOTICE file
      must remain in every copy of the Software and of any Derivative Work.

  3.5 This section does not restrict:
      (a) use that is not Production Use, including the sample settlement
          provider shipped for demonstrations and tests, and the presence in
          the source of the provider interface through which the Sera.cx
          Protocol and that sample provider are connected;
      (b) fiat on-ramps and off-ramps, bank payouts and the partners You
          choose for them, except where used as described in section 3.3;
      (c) payouts that require no exchange because the funding stablecoin and
          the payout stablecoin are the same;
      (d) Your choice of screening, identity, statutory, notification,
          database, hosting or wallet providers; or
      (e) any exception the Licensor publishes in writing in the Protocol
          Register for a pair, network or situation the Sera.cx Protocol does
          not serve.

  3.6 Where the Sera.cx Protocol does not serve a pair or network and no
      exception under 3.5(e) applies, the payout may be deferred or paid in a
      stablecoin the Sera.cx Protocol does serve, or paid in fiat. It may not
      be routed through another venue, except to the extent, and for the
      period, that a law applying to You requires the payment to be made in a
      form or by a time that cannot be met through the Sera.cx Protocol, in
      which case You must give the Licensor written notice within ten
      business days describing the law, the pair or network, and the volume
      concerned.

  3.7 You must keep records sufficient to show that each Settlement Function
      in Production Use complied with this section, for six years after the
      run concerned, and must within fifteen business days of the Licensor's
      written request provide the on-chain transaction references and the
      settlement configuration for the Production runs the request
      identifies. The Licensor may make such a request no more than twice in
      any twelve months unless it has reasonable grounds to suspect a breach.

  3.8 Sections 3.1 to 3.7 apply to every Derivative Work and to every
      recipient of the Software or a Derivative Work, however many times it
      is copied, modified or redistributed.

  3.9 Sections 2.1, 2.2 and 3.1 to 3.4 together define the scope of the
      copyright licence granted. An act outside that scope is both an
      infringement of the Licensor's copyright and a breach of this
      agreement, and the Licensor may pursue either or both.

