  modifying, distributing or making Production Use of the Software or a
  Derivative Work. If You act for a legal entity, You confirm that You have
  authority to bind it. If You do not accept these terms, You have no licence
  and must not do any of those acts.

5. Redistribution

  5.1 Any copy of the Software or of a Derivative Work that You distribute,
      in source or compiled form, must be in Compliant Form, must be
      accompanied by this licence and the NOTICE file, unchanged, and must
      state conspicuously that it is licensed under the Sera.cx Payroll
      Source Licence. Each recipient receives a licence directly from the
      Licensor under this licence.

  5.2 You may offer additional terms for Your own additions to a Derivative
      Work, and may charge for Your product, provided those terms do not
      conflict with this licence and do not purport to relieve any recipient
      of section 3.

  5.3 You may not relicense the Software or a Derivative Work under any other
      licence, open source or otherwise.

6. Termination

  6.1 Any act outside the scope of section 2, and any breach of section 3,
      terminates all rights granted to You under this licence automatically,
      immediately and permanently, without notice and without any period to
      cure. That termination is irrevocable. After it, any use, copying,
      modification or distribution of the Software or of a Derivative Work by
      You is unlicensed and infringes the Licensor's copyright. Rights can be
      restored only by a new written licence signed by the Licensor.

  6.2 Any other breach terminates this licence if it is not cured within
      thirty days of written notice from the Licensor.

  6.3 For thirty days after termination You may complete, in Compliant Form
      and through the Sera.cx Protocol only, the payouts that were approved
      and funded before the date of termination, so that the people being
      paid are not harmed. No other right survives.

  6.4 Termination of Your licence does not terminate the licence of any
      recipient who received the Software or a Derivative Work from You and
      remains in compliance.

  6.5 Sections 3.4 (as to notices), 3.7, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11 and 13 survive
      termination.

7. Remedies and enforcement

  7.1 You acknowledge that a breach of section 3, or an act outside the scope
      of section 2, would cause the Licensor harm that damages alone cannot
      adequately compensate, and that the Licensor is entitled, in addition
      to every other remedy, to injunctive relief, specific performance and
      delivery up or destruction of non-compliant copies, in any court of
      competent jurisdiction, without proof of special damage and, to the
      extent the law allows, without the need to post a bond or other
      security.

  7.2 The Licensor's remedies are cumulative. They include damages or an
      account of profits for copyright infringement, damages for breach of
      contract, and recovery of the Licensor's costs of enforcement,
      including legal fees, on a full indemnity basis to the extent the law
      allows. The parties agree that the fees the Sera.cx Protocol would have
      earned on each Settlement Function performed in breach of section 3,
      at the Licensor's published fee schedule at the time, are a reasonable
      minimum measure of the Licensor's loss from that breach, without
      prejudice to any larger claim.

  7.3 The Licensor may pursue any person who copies, modifies, distributes or
      makes Production Use of the Software or a Derivative Work outside the
      scope of this licence, whether or not that person received it from the
      Licensor and whether or not that person accepted this licence.

  7.4 No failure or delay by the Licensor in enforcing any term is a waiver
      of it, and no waiver is effective unless in writing signed by the
      Licensor.

